{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hackjunction.app/participate/45/hackerpacks/64"}}{\fldrslt \cf0 \
BY CRACI\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 CRACI Platform\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Resources Every team gets free access to the CRACI platform for the whole event, CI/CD build minutes included. CRACI runners are GitHub Actions compatible, so you can keep your existing workflows and switch a job over in one line. As your builds run, CRACI records every external dependency they pull in and produces verifiable CycloneDX SBOMs, including packages restored from caches, and AI fixes can patch vulnerabilities automatically based on that exact build data. Everything is open to you through the CRACI API, and our docs ship with agent skills so you can work with them in your AI coding tools. Our whole team is on site to help you get set up and to go deep on supply chain security. List of technologies that we are bringing: \'96 Free access to the CRACI platform during the event (platform.craci.com) \'96 CI/CD build minutes on CRACI's GitHub Actions-compatible runners \'96 Build-time CycloneDX SBOMs with completeness data per job and per cache \'96 AI fixes: automated vulnerability fixes grounded in exact build data \'96 The CRACI API: SBOMs, OCI image and cache provenance, network traces, job logs and compute usage \'96 Documentation, examples and agent skills: https://docs.craci.com/ \'96 Five mentors from the CRACI team on site all weekend Claim your free compute Every team gets 1000\'80 credits to the CRACI platform for the whole event. These can be used for CI/CD or any compute need you require. Setup takes about ten minutes. 1. Get your invite code You need the Junction invite code to create your team's organization on CRACI. Get it either way: 
\f1\b Discord:
\f0\b0  Ask in the 
\fs24 #craci
\fs26  channel on the Junction Discord. 
\f1\b CRACI booth:
\f0\b0  Come say hi. We'll give you the code and help with setup on the spot. Only one person per team needs to do steps 2 to 4. Invite your teammates afterwards. 2. Sign up and create your organization Go to platform.craci.com and sign up. Create an organization for your team and enter the Junction invite code. 3. Connect GitHub In CRACI, go to 
\f1\b Settings \uc0\u8594  Builds
\f0\b0  and start the 
\f1\b Install GitHub
\f0\b0  flow. CRACI walks you through creating its GitHub App and installing it on your GitHub organization or account. Grant the App access to the repositories you'll build: all repositories, or a selected set. Wait until the connection shows 
\f1\b configured
\f0\b0 . You can change repository access later on GitHub under 
\f1\b Settings \uc0\u8594  GitHub Apps \u8594  CRACI \u8594  Configure
\f0\b0 . 4. Run your first build on CRACI After connecting the app, any workflow file with runs-on: craci will be running on the CRACI platform. The default runner size is 2 vCPUs and 6GB RAM. 
\fs24 jobs: build: runs-on: craci steps: - uses: actions/checkout@v4 - run: make build 
\fs26 Push, and the job runs on CRACI. Open the build in the platform to see what it pulled in. Need a bigger machine? Add the setup step first: 
\fs24 steps: - uses: cracicorp/setup@v1 with: size: "8" # 1\'9632 units; each unit is 1 vCPU and 3 GB RAM. Default is 2. - uses: actions/checkout@v4 
\fs26 You can also point your agent at our migration skill for migrating old workflows or when creating new ones: https://docs.craci.com/skills/craci/SKILL.md 5. Get an API token An organization admin can create a token under 
\f1\b Settings \uc0\u8594  API tokens
\f0\b0 . The token is shown only once, so store it somewhere safe. Call the API at 
\fs24 https://api.craci.com
\fs26  with 
\fs24 Authorization: Bearer $CRACI_API_TOKEN
\fs26 . The full OpenAPI spec is at api.craci.com/openapi.json . Resources If you or your agent needs more info, check out docs.craci.com or come yap with us at the booth! (3rd next to the stage)\
}}\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hackjunction.app/participate/45/hackerpacks/63"}}{\fldrslt \cf0 \
