{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hackjunction.app/participate/45/hackerpacks/59"}}{\fldrslt \cf0 \
BY IRONSHARD\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 IronShard (Datasets for other challenges)\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 What is IronShard? IronShard is a next-generation cloud object storage service built for developers and AI agents. Its key features include: AI-native storage: Access and manage the same buckets using AI agents through MCP or traditional applications through the S3-compatible API. Zero-copy bucket forking: Instantly create independent, writable branches of existing datasets without duplicating the underlying data. Intelligent multi-cloud storage: Data is encrypted, erasure-coded, and distributed across a global mesh of 200+ storage regions operated by 10+ providers, with automatic optimization of placement, redundancy, performance, and costs. How can you use IronShard during the hackathon? IronShard provides several ways to work with challenge data and build your solutions: Access challenge datasets: Where applicable, input data is preloaded into read-only IronShard buckets. Fork datasets with one click: Create your own writable bucket from a challenge dataset, instantly and without copying the original data. Create your own buckets: Create as many additional buckets as you need for your solution. Connect AI agents and S3 tools: All buckets (read-only, forked, or manually created) are accessible through MCP for AI agents and through standard S3-compatible tools and libraries. Store and submit large artifacts: If your solution includes trained AI models, datasets, or other files too large for a regular GitHub repository (which allows max 100 MiB per file), store them in an IronShard bucket. Include the bucket and object references in your submission. Hackathon judges will be given read access to these artifacts.\
}}\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
