{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hackjunction.app/participate/45/hackerpacks/50"}}{\fldrslt \cf0 \
BY SCAILAB\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 SCAILAB: Scaipipe Access\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Scailab builds tools for creating computer vision models quickly and in a controlled way for robotics, industrial automation and autonomous systems. Our platform, Scaipipe, covers the full loop in one place. You can import and annotate your own images, generate labelled synthetic training data from 3D scenes built in a visual node editor, then train, evaluate and improve detection, segmentation and tracking models. Scene generation, labelling and analysis run right in your browser, so you don\'92t need a GPU to get started, and AI agents like Claude can drive the whole pipeline through Scaipipe\'92s built-in MCP server. During Junction you\'92ll be among the platform\'92s early users, and your feedback will help shape what we build next.\
}}\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hackjunction.app/participate/45/hackerpacks/49"}}{\fldrslt \cf0 \
BY EXA\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Exa Credits\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 What we'll bring:
\f0\b0  Every participant will get $50 in Exa Credits and access to our full API for the event. This includes the Search API with fast, balanced and deep research modes, and the Contents API for full page text, highlights, summaries and crawling a site's subpages. Teams can filter results by date, domain and category (such as news, research papers, companies, people and personal websites), request results as structured JSON, and retrieve past versions of web pages. We will also provide Websets for building verified lists of people, companies and opportunities, Monitors for recurring searches, our hosted MCP server, and Python and JavaScript SDKs. Our demo gallery at demos.exa.ai has working examples teams can build from. Exa engineers will be on site throughout the event to help with technical questions and project ideas, and there will also be a discord to receive asynchronous advice}}}